sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant T as Track.jsx
    participant RA as RapidAPI<br/>Edamam Food Database
    participant API as Express<br/>POST /track
    participant DB as MongoDB<br/>trackings
    participant D as Diet.jsx

    U->>T: Type a food name and click Search
    T->>RA: GET /auto-complete?q=query
    RA-->>T: ["name 1", "name 2", ...]
    par One request per suggestion (Promise.all)
        T->>RA: GET /api/food-database/v2/parser?ingr=name
        RA-->>T: hints[0].food.nutrients (per 100 g)
    end
    T->>T: Remove duplicates with a Map<br/>key = label-image-calories
    T-->>U: Show food cards (values per 100 g)

    U->>T: Enter quantity in grams
    T->>T: value x grams / 100 for each nutrient
    U->>T: Click Track
    T->>T: Build item: userId, random foodId, foodName,<br/>scaled details, quantity (default 100)
    T->>API: POST /track (Bearer token)
    API->>API: verifyToken, then eatenDate defaults to<br/>today as DD-MM-YYYY (server clock)
    API->>DB: trackingModel.create(item)
    API-->>T: 201 created document
    Note over T: Result is only written to the console. No UI message.

    U->>D: Open Diet page and pick a date
    D->>API: GET /track/:userid/M-D-YYYY (no auth needed)
    API->>API: Parses the date as D-M-YYYY
    API->>DB: find({ userId, eatenDate }).populate("userId")
    API-->>D: Matching entries (often empty or the wrong day)
    Note over D,API: Known bug: month and day are swapped.<br/>The populated user includes the password hash.
